- Popup errors on `chrome://` / `edge://` tabs (unchecked `runtime.lastError`, null listeners) — inject only via `getActiveInjectableTab()`; duration helpers hoisted; expected Google 401 re-auth no longer `console.warn`s (Chrome lists warns as extension errors). Manifest bumped to `1.1.4`.
- YouTube embed in popup failed with error 153 (no Referer on extension sub_frames) — fixed with `declarativeNetRequestWithHostAccess` rule setting `Referer: https://www.youtube.com/` for `youtube.com/embed/` initiated by the extension; CSP `frame-src` allows YouTube.
- View history playlist rebuilt as v2 overlay (102:1204): replaced legacy chip modal; added `watched_at`; fixed panel + sticky pager; newest-first; row exit animation.
- First-time Wrong URL (143:4558): never-logged-in + non-watch runs full onboarding with `authFlowKind=new-wrong-url`, lands on `#wrongUrlFallAnim` (image BG + hardcoded modal) instead of Schedule; `#newUserWrongUrl` kept for returning logged-out only.
- Slot algorithm v1: scores table separate from prefs; rescans never overwrite selection; opportunistic rescan on prefs open if scores >30d stale; Trigger B (cron) deferred until Google refresh tokens exist server-side.
- Slot algorithm hardening (stress test pass): `fetchFreeBusyRange` returned `[]` on 403/500 and on per-calendar errors inside a 200, so any Calendar outage scored the user's whole calendar as free and suggested bogus slots — now throws. Degraded per-month fallback scored unfetched months as free — now scores `coveredRanges` only. A popup closed mid-scan left a `running` row that blocked every future scan forever — now a 10-min TTL. `not_before` was written but never read (unbounded retries against Google) — now honoured for opportunistic rescans. Multi-year freeBusy blocks expanded into ~36.5k day buckets (101ms for one event) — now clamped to the window (1.3ms). `mergeIntervals` returned `[undefined]` when every input was unusable. Day/bucket ranking used max across the other axis, so every weekday of a booked calendar tied — now mean, with `avgFreeRatio` as tiebreak. Deleted dead `analyzeCalendarPrefs` + duplicate local `prefsAnalysisWindow`.
- `scanAndScore` Edge Function fixed: it used `setHours()` for bucket boundaries while running in UTC, so an IST user's "Morning (6–9)" would have been scored as 11:30–14:30 local — every score row in the wrong bucket. Now takes a validated IANA `timeZone` and resolves boundaries through `Intl` (`tz.mjs`). Also carried over the client hardening it had missed: per-calendar `errors` inside a 200 no longer read as a free calendar, busy intervals are clamped to the window, `mergeIntervals` can't return `[undefined]`, `freeRatio` is clamped to [0,1], scan lock/backoff is honoured, and a failed score upsert now marks the run `failed` instead of reporting success. Dropped the `URL` global shadow, unused `WEEKDAY_KEYS`, and reflect-any-origin CORS.
- **Security pass (2026-08-05).** Four orphan Edge Functions were live and dangerous; all four are now `410` stubs with `verify_jwt` on. (1) `exchange-token` ran with `verify_jwt: false` and `ACAO: *`, giving the public internet `/exchange` (any auth code → Google tokens using our **client secret**, then a service-role DB write), `/refresh` (any refresh token → a fresh access token, again on our client secret), and `/debug` (an unauthenticated service-role insert). **Rotate `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`** — it backed a public endpoint for ~16 months. (2) `send-reminder-email` had no `serve()` handler at all: `main()` ran at module load, so a cold start alone mass-mailed every auth user. (3) `sendDailyEmails` did no in-function auth, so the public anon key triggered a mailout to all users. (4) `sendReferralNotification` was an abandoned twin of the live slug carrying the same body-trust flaw. Live functions fixed: `sendreferralnotification` took `referrerId` / `friendName` / `referralCode` straight from the request body, so any signed-in user could mail **any** user arbitrary HTML from our sending domain (phishing), and probe which user ids exist via 404-vs-200 — it now derives referrer, code and friend name from the caller's own redemption row, HTML-escapes every interpolation, and marks `notified_at` so it can't be replayed; both live functions stopped reflecting arbitrary `Origin`. Client fixes: a referrer's Google display name was written to `innerHTML` in the privileged popup (CSP blocked script, but not injected markup) → escaped; history row `href` was escaped but not scheme-checked, so a `javascript:` URL would still fire on click → `safeExternalUrl`; `background.js` answered runtime messages from any installed extension (`login` opens a Google consent window) → sender check; the OAuth `nonce` came from `Math.random()` → `crypto.randomUUID()`; manifest dropped `web_accessible_resources` (fingerprinting), the stale `oauth2` block, and a scope string sitting in `host_permissions`.
- History playlist restyled to Figma 116:4021 / 4236 / 4374: page size 4 → **5**, pager label regained the `| Page X of Y` counter that 102:1204 had dropped, filter pill 140 → 128px, nav buttons 32 → 28px with 14px icons, chip rotation −2° → −1°, panel radius 16 → 12. The hardcoded `--history-panel-h: 379px` is gone — the panel is `height: auto` over a 5-row list slot, which is what actually kept it from jumping. Markup was already correct; this was CSS plus three lines of JS.
- Modal padding unified at **12 on all four sides**. The 12/12/8 variant survived in the history panel and the Permissions/Analyzing auth sheets, and the `--pad-modal-top/x/bottom` trio existed only to express that asymmetry (all three were already 12px, so they bought nothing but a way to reintroduce it). Tokens deleted, all six call sites now use `var(--space-3)`, and `tests/selfcheck.js` fails if either the 12/12/8 pattern or the tokens come back. Gaps are 16 everywhere except the expanded prefs sheet, which keeps 20 per Figma 36:2189.
- **Shared white-modal motion.** History, logged-in Wrong URL, offline, and delete confirm use `.wl-modal` / `.wl-modal-panel` (feedback uses `.feedback-overlay`). Backdrop fades while the panel scales `0.96 → 1` and rises 8px, 240ms ease-in-out, reversed on close via `openOverlay()` / `closeOverlay()` (`MODAL_ANIM_MS` = 240).
- History row hover controls animate now: they were `display: none` → `flex`, which can't transition. The actions column opens from `max-width: 0` to its content width (38 or 84 via `:has(.history-action + .history-action)`) with the 12px gap carried as an animatable `margin-left` — the row's own `gap` is 0, otherwise a collapsed column would still steal 12px from the title. Buttons slide in from the right inside the clipped column, and the title reflows shorter, matching the Figma hover state. Page turns and tab switches repaint behind a 160ms opacity cross-fade (`repaintHistoryPageFaded`); typing in search still repaints instantly.
- **Top nav + profile menu (218:1834 / 116:4508 / 228:2171).** Dropped the Figma Glass emulation on the two nav buttons — `backdrop-filter`, the light rims, the `#schedGlassRefract` SVG filter and the `--sched-glass-*` tokens are all gone, leaving flat `#000@25%` circles with white icons. The hamburger became the user's Google photo, with `Icon/avatar-fallback-koala.png` behind an `onerror` handler because Google's `lh3` URLs 404 once a photo is changed. The menu replaces the scheduling sheet rather than floating over it. Two bugs found only by rendering it: `SLOT_PERSONAS` keyed by bucket **label** never matched, since `SLOT_RANGES` labels use en dashes and the copy used hyphens (now keyed by start hour, with a self-check that every bucket has a badge); and `.profile-persona[hidden]` needed an explicit `display: none`, because `.onb-chip`'s `inline-flex` beats the `hidden` attribute. The trend strip also has to stay one line — at 12px padding the sentence plus both sparkles is 281px in a 276px box, and wrapping pushed the text up behind the stats card, out of view.
- Pain↔Promise copy morph added: the heading slides ±24px across the crossfade and the single Next morphs into Back+Next. First attempt animated only the incoming screen, which rendered two "Next" labels side by side for the whole 450ms — the outgoing button was still full width underneath. Fixed by giving both screens the same collapsed/expanded geometry, and by targeting the secondary's natural half width rather than 50%, which had left the two primaries ~6px out of step.
- Onboarding card carousel reworked: bounce easing dropped for `ease-in-out`, and the two cards involved in a step now scale as well as fade (leaving 100→90%, arriving 90→100%). The ticker dots looked static through a page change for a subtler reason — the dots aren't shared between slides, and each slide's markup already marks its own dot active, so the incoming ticker faded in already finished. `goTo` now rewinds it to the outgoing step with transitions off, then animates both tickers together under the crossfade.
- Referral UI deleted. It had no entry point in the new menu, `openReferFriendModal` was already unreachable, and `openEnterReferralModal` auto-popped the legacy chip modal on first login — which would now land on top of the new profile UI. ~320 lines of JS, 120 lines of CSS and the popup's only `sendreferralnotification` call went with it; the tables, the Edge Function and the logout wipe stay.
- Legacy v1 `#scheduleBtn` CSS deleted (52px orange button with a 6px bottom border, plus two dead `.confirm-btn.with-icon` shimmer rules — `#scheduleBtn` hasn't carried those classes since v2). The `#scheduleBtn.onb-btn` block existed only to beat it and restated `.onb-btn` almost verbatim, but with a 4px shell instead of 3px, so the schedule CTA was subtly *not* the same button as "Yes, I allow". All three blocks are gone; the CTA is now plain `.onb-btn` and computes identically to every other modal primary.
- **Schedule success rebuilt to Figma 380:5065**, then simplified: tried same-`#schedSheet` morph + skeleton bridge (felt jerky); replaced with a separate `#successPanel` that slides up / down. Selfcheck guards `--success-slide-ms` ↔ `SUCCESS_SLIDE_MS` and rejects the deleted morph helpers.
- **Design critique pass 2 comment triage (2026-08-12):** worked through the user's replies on all 17 second-batch comment threads, then got answers on the three open decisions and finished them:
  - **Renamed-video detection — built.** The Forced tab was meant to cover removed, renamed, *and* time-drifted videos, but code only ever detected the first and third. `loadHistoryItems`'s existing per-row oEmbed call (already used to catch a removed video) now also reads the live title and flags `forced = true` if it differs from the stored one — joining the same "Scheduled for..." bucket as a time-drift row, no separate visual state. Empty-state copy on all three tabs now says "...changed, were renamed, or were removed...". Guarded by a new `tests/selfcheck.js` assertion (`meta.title !== item.title`).
  - **Grey button gradient — Figma had drifted, not code.** Batch-fixed 112 nodes `#cccccc` → `#d9d9d9`. Lone-CTA auth screens switched to purple primary in Figma. **Resolved — do not re-open.**
  - **Pain/Promise CTA — kept "Next".** Figma frames updated. **Resolved — do not re-open.**
  Also fixed two more mock-only issues found while re-checking: the Watched empty-state subtext still had the original "Videos mark as watched" typo in Figma (grammar fix had only landed in code, not the mock) — now reads "marked"; and the Forced empty-state subtext still trailed off ("Any videos deleted from google calendar") — reworded to match the shipped copy. Delete-confirm mock's mismatched video title and un-fixed run-on sentence were also brought in line with the already-fixed shipped code. Double-checked the delete-sessions confirm's button order (flagged as backwards in the original critique) — it was already "Go Back" then "Yes, delete" left-to-right, so no change was needed there.
- **Design critique pass 2 follow-through (2026-08-12):** acted on the two biggest gaps the pass flagged. Built `#failOverlay`/`#failPanel` — a real v2 schedule-failure sheet (`showScheduleFailModal`/`closeScheduleFailModal`) reusing the success overlay's shell with a pink/red gradient and a `.fail-card-error` line, replacing the dead v1 `#failureScreen` that auto-hid after 5s with a plain text line and no retry. Built the two-line empty state (grey skeleton illustration + heading + subtext) for all three history tabs, worded per what each tab actually tracks — the Forced copy deliberately omits "renamed" since title changes aren't tracked, only calendar-time drift and removal. Switched the profile trend window from 30 days to 7 (`TREND_WINDOW_DAYS`) and its copy to "since last week" to match the Figma mocks (dropped 30-day here made "since last month" copy just wrong, not a rounding choice), and deleted the now-unused sparkle icons/CSS since the copy already states the direction. Found one more `[hidden]` CSS bug in the process — `.history-pager`'s `display: flex` beat the `hidden` attribute exactly like `.profile-persona` once did, so an empty tab kept showing "0-0 of 0 rows"; fixed with a `.history-pager[hidden] { display: none }` override. All four are guarded by new `tests/selfcheck.js` assertions.
- **Auth warn banners rebuilt in CSS (2026-08-12):** replaced three PNG exports (`auth-warn-banner-privacy.png`, `auth-warn-banner.png`, `auth-warn-banner-why.png`) with one `.auth-warn-banner` component — inline Tabler info icon + Sub-Text, tokens `--color-warning-*` / `--shadow-auth-warn`. `setAnalyzeBanner()` no longer toggles img nodes; `.is-live` handles scan-error wrap. Parity 100/100 vs Figma `418:1083` / `171:800` / `171:934`. PNGs deleted from repo; selfcheck guards against reintroduction.
- **Design critique pass 2 (2026-08-12), 18 prefs/profile/schedule-outcome/history/session/feedback screens vs code:** ~~Biggest gap: schedule failure had no v2 UI~~ **built** (`#failOverlay`/`#failPanel`). ~~History empty states not built~~ **built** (two-line heading + subtext + skeleton illustration per tab). Remaining mock gaps: the **history Watched and Forced tab mocks show the wrong row copy** — both were seemingly cloned from the Scheduled tab without updating the per-row subtitle, so they show "Scheduled for.../Upcoming in.../Missed" instead of what those tabs actually render (Watched: `Moved to Watched X ago` only; Forced: `Scheduled for...` drift or dimmed "Video removed by the Channel" only, never Upcoming/Missed). The mark-watched-sessions and delete-sessions confirm screens are speculative, tied to the not-yet-built multi-session-scheduling feature (real mark-watched has no confirm step at all; real delete only ever removes one video). Time-preferences mock has 3 of 6 slot labels with swapped AM/PM (e.g. "9AM -12 AM" instead of "9AM - 12PM") plus a wrong night-owl parenthetical — confirmed **Figma-only drift**, the shipped `TIME_CHIP_LABELS` (popup.js:411-416) and night-owl copy (popup.html:920) were already correct. ~~Profile trend used 30-day window~~ **fixed** — code now uses 7-day window (`TREND_WINDOW_DAYS`) with "since last week" copy. Fixed live in code (not just Figma): `success-heading-line` "Google calendar" → "Google Calendar" (popup.html:1200); `deleteBody` run-on "This can't be undone it'll be removed…" → em dash added (popup.html:1107); `feedbackTitle` "Share us your feedback" (not valid English) → "Give us your feedback" (popup.html:1073); day-prefs Sunday banner "Go out have fun :)" → "Go out, have fun :)" (popup.html:874). Renamed all ~515 auto-named "Frame ####"/"Group ####" layers across these 18 screens to semantic names matching the code's structure, and the 18 screen roots to `correctURL*` ids (two marked `_NOT_BUILT` where there's no code counterpart at all). Posted 17 pinned Figma comments, all prefixed "🤖 Cursor Agent". **Known tooling limitation:** no API to mark Figma comments resolved — fixed items are prefixed "Fixed" in-thread; ticking "Resolved" is manual.
- **Design critique pass (2026-08-12), 14 onboarding/auth screens vs code:** unified auth retry CTA to "Try again" + primary `.onb-btn` on all four error sheets. Fixed copy bugs, added `prefersReducedMotion()` gating on auth MP4s, corrected `--tracking-label` to 1.6%. ~~Left open: grey gradient end-stop and Pain/Promise CTA~~ **both resolved** in design critique pass 2 triage (grey → `#d9d9d9` in Figma; CTA kept "Next").

